segments, Pipeline and Gathering. The Pipeline segment owns and operates interstate and intrastate natural gas pipelines, storage systems, and natural gas gathering lateral pipelines. This segment also engages in the transportation and storage of natural gas for intermediate and end-user customers. The Gathering segment owns and operates gas gathering systems. This segment is involved in the collection of natural gas for delivery to plants for treating, to gathering pipelines for further gathering, or to pipelines for transportation; and associated ancillary services, including compression, dehydration, gas treatment, water impoundment, water transportation, water disposal, and sand mining. It serves natural gas producers, local distribution companies, electric power generators, industrials, and national marketers. The company was incorporated in 2021 and is headquartered in Detroit, Michigan.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David J. Slater | CEO & Executive Chairman | Age 58 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 588 people. Revenue per employee of $2.1M ranks in the above the sector median among Energy peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $750K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $44K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["DT Midstream, Inc. is a large-cap energy business with a $12.2B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $441M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 35 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.97\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 2.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 4.5\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 206% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.06031353737908},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 34% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Financial quality scores above most Energy peers","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Investment Analysts\u2019 Upgrades for November 13th (ADSK, DAVE, DPZ, DTM, ECL, ENGN, LFTO, NMAX, NMG)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/investment-analysts-upgrades-for-november-13th-adsk-dave-dpz-dtm-ecl-engn-lfto-nmax-nmg.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794595487.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.856,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"How Dt Midstream Inc. (DTM) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/151/How_Dt_Midstream_Inc._DTM_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_111026083201_1794360721.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794360721.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Dividend Affirmation Altering The Investment Case For DT Midstream (DTM)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-dtm/dt-midstream/news/is-dividend-affirmation-altering-the-investment-case-for-dt","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794299104.416,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"DT Midstream (DTM), The Latest Update Raises A Bigger Question","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-dtm/dt-midstream/news/dt-midstream-dtm-the-latest-update-raises-a-bigger-question","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794140877.265,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.852,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Price Cut: Why Has Dart Mining (ASX:DTM) Accepted Less for Indigo Metals